      "content": "Imagine a mother walking two hours each day, her young children trailing behind, not to school, but to a muddy, contaminated water source. Our intervention changes that narrative entirely; clean water means fewer debilitating waterborne illnesses, directly allowing children, especially girls, to stay in classrooms instead of fetching water. This newfound time translates into stronger local businesses and healthier futures for entire villages. We aren't just building pipes; we are replacing the daily anxiety of sickness and scarcity with the simple, profound stability of reliable, clean hydration.",
      "source": "target",
